    {
      "id": "g1zcErPlgFUf0nKrR2z76",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 746.7822590977696,
      "y": 8989.068327774046,
      "width": 1045,
      "height": 1025,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3w",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1375797883,
      "version": 236,
      "versionNonce": 755020277,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785475262065,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "One of the most common interview topics.\nImagine the access token never expires.\nIf someone steals it:\n    Attacker -> Uses Token Forever\n\nThat's dangerous.\nInstead:\n    Access Token -> 15 Minutes\n    Refresh Token -> 7 days\n\nFlow:\n    Login -> Access Token -> 15 minutes pass -> 401 Unauthorized -> Client Sends Refresh Token \n        -> Backend Verifies -> New Access Token\n\nThe user doesn't have to log in again.\n\nAPIs We'll Build -> For our project, we'll eventually implement:\n\nPOST   /api/auth/signup\nPOST   /api/auth/verify-email\nPOST   /api/auth/login\nPOST   /api/auth/refresh\nPOST   /api/auth/logout\nPOST   /api/auth/forgot-password\nPOST   /api/auth/reset-password\nGET    /api/users/me\n\nWe'll keep these endpoints stable as the project grows.\n\nDesign Exercise\nSuppose a user signs up.\nWhich tables change?\nThink before answering.\nExpected thought process:\n    Signup -> User table\nnew user created\n\nLater, after the user creates their first organization:\nOrganization -> OrganizationMember (user becomes owner)\n\nNotice how the authentication system and the organization system are related but separate.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "One of the most common interview topics.\nImagine the access token never expires.\nIf someone steals it:\n    Attacker -> Uses Token Forever\n\nThat's dangerous.\nInstead:\n    Access Token -> 15 Minutes\n    Refresh Token -> 7 days\n\nFlow:\n    Login -> Access Token -> 15 minutes pass -> 401 Unauthorized -> Client Sends Refresh Token \n        -> Backend Verifies -> New Access Token\n\nThe user doesn't have to log in again.\n\nAPIs We'll Build -> For our project, we'll eventually implement:\n\nPOST   /api/auth/signup\nPOST   /api/auth/verify-email\nPOST   /api/auth/login\nPOST   /api/auth/refresh\nPOST   /api/auth/logout\nPOST   /api/auth/forgot-password\nPOST   /api/auth/reset-password\nGET    /api/users/me\n\nWe'll keep these endpoints stable as the project grows.\n\nDesign Exercise\nSuppose a user signs up.\nWhich tables change?\nThink before answering.\nExpected thought process:\n    Signup -> User table\nnew user created\n\nLater, after the user creates their first organization:\nOrganization -> OrganizationMember (user becomes owner)\n\nNotice how the authentication system and the organization system are related but separate.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "mL63D5l8Lrho4KGfzo8fv",
